WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:18.907
The next morning, the Earthworms rode their bikes to the end of Old Church Road.

2
00:00:18.908 --> 00:00:20.729
Katie was confused.

3
00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:24.618
"Do we go this way or that way?" she asked.

4
00:00:24.619 --> 00:00:27.231
"We need a GPS!"

5
00:00:27.232 --> 00:00:29.499
But Luke knew the way.

6
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.687
He led them over an old bridge and down a dirt road.

7
00:00:33.688 --> 00:00:36.182
"We're getting close!"

8
00:00:36.183 --> 00:00:40.761
A few moments later, they stopped in front of an old house.

9
00:00:40.762 --> 00:00:42.784
"This is it," he said.

10
00:00:42.785 --> 00:00:45.032
It looked deserted.

11
00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:48.375
"Creepy," said Katie.

12
00:00:48.376 --> 00:00:52.149
"Nobody lives here," said Emily.

13
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:55.963
"Let's go home," said AJ.

14
00:00:55.964 --> 00:00:59.231
"Shh. Listen," said Emily.

15
00:00:59.232 --> 00:01:05.634
Someone was singing.

16
00:01:05.635 --> 00:01:09.053
They left their bikes and followed the voice.

17
00:01:09.054 --> 00:01:14.817
An old woman was hanging clothes to dry, singing as she worked.

18
00:01:14.818 --> 00:01:21.209
She fastened the last piece to the line, picked up her basket, and turned around.

19
00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:24.610
"Who are you?" she snapped.

20
00:01:24.611 --> 00:01:28.143
"She seems crabby," thought Katie.

21
00:01:28.144 --> 00:01:31.334
"We're the Earthworms!" said AJ.

22
00:01:31.335 --> 00:01:33.830
Emily pushed her brother.

23
00:01:33.831 --> 00:01:36.672
"I'm Emily," she said.

24
00:01:36.673 --> 00:01:40.656
"Luke." "AJ." "Katie."

25
00:01:40.657 --> 00:01:42.861
"What are you doing here?

26
00:01:42.862 --> 00:01:47.476
I never have visitors," the old woman said.

27
00:01:47.477 --> 00:01:51.946
"We're on a scavenger hunt," Katie replied.

28
00:01:51.947 --> 00:01:53.981
The woman looked doubtful.

29
00:01:53.982 --> 00:01:57.391
"What are you hunting out here?"

30
00:01:57.392 --> 00:02:00.451
"You!" said AJ.

31
00:02:00.452 --> 00:02:04.989
"The oldest person in Willow Creek," said Emily.

32
00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:09.510
"You're Ms. Cora Mae Henderson, right?" said Katie.

33
00:02:09.511 --> 00:02:13.499
"Your brother drew us a map so we could find you."

34
00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:18.652
"My brother is a busybody," said Ms. Henderson.

35
00:02:18.653 --> 00:02:22.497
"He has a Model T!" said AJ.

36
00:02:22.498 --> 00:02:25.116
Ms. Henderson finally smiled.

37
00:02:25.117 --> 00:02:29.721
"Oh, yes. I've heard all about it.

38
00:02:29.722 --> 00:02:33.971
Brother says he will take me for a ride soon."

39
00:02:33.972 --> 00:02:36.991
Ms. Henderson looked up at the back porch.

40
00:02:36.992 --> 00:02:41.698
"If you don't mind, I'd like to sit down."

41
00:02:41.699 --> 00:02:45.152
When everyone was comfortable, Luke said,

42
00:02:45.153 --> 00:02:50.202
"Your brother says his Model T was the first car in Willow Creek."

43
00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:53.770
"That could be true," she said.

44
00:02:53.771 --> 00:02:59.713
"I was a school girl when Randolph Patterson bought that Model T.

45
00:02:59.714 --> 00:03:02.582
Folks didn't like it though.

46
00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:08.512
When that car raced down the road, dust clouds filled the air.

47
00:03:08.513 --> 00:03:10.274
You couldn't breathe.

48
00:03:10.275 --> 00:03:15.026
The farmers, like my daddy, said the dust hurt the crops.

49
00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:20.932
And if it was washing day, the ladies had to take everything off the line.

50
00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:25.113
They had to wash their laundry all over again."

51
00:03:25.114 --> 00:03:31.394
"Your brother is going to drive his Model T in the Willow Creek birthday parade," said Luke.

52
00:03:31.395 --> 00:03:36.809
"Willow Creek is turning 150 years old," said Katie.

53
00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:41.371
"My, my. Time passes quickly.

54
00:03:41.372 --> 00:03:46.841
When Willow Creek turned fifty, I was just a little girl.

55
00:03:46.842 --> 00:03:54.391
When it turned one hundred, I had gray hair!" Ms. Henderson laughed.

56
00:03:54.392 --> 00:03:59.967
"And now the town is 150 already?"

57
00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:04.808
"Yep. And we're going to be in the parade," said Emily.

58
00:04:04.809 --> 00:04:08.556
"You could be in it too!" said Katie.

59
00:04:08.557 --> 00:04:12.737
"Oh, no, I don't go to town anymore,"

60
00:04:12.738 --> 00:04:15.849
said Ms. Henderson, shaking her head.

61
00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:19.079
"It's too busy now."

62
00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:23.557
"You could ride in the Model T!" said AJ.

63
00:04:23.558 --> 00:04:26.539
"We're going," said Emily.

64
00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:32.388
"Well, I have to think about it," said Ms. Henderson.

65
00:04:32.389 --> 00:04:38.605
"Ms. Henderson, will you write a note for our scavenger bag?" asked Katie.

66
00:04:38.606 --> 00:04:44.901
Ms. Henderson smiled. "I did many scavenger hunts when I was a girl."

67
00:04:44.902 --> 00:04:47.660
She happily wrote out a note.

68
00:04:47.661 --> 00:04:51.704
It said: My name is Cora Mae Henderson.

69
00:04:51.705 --> 00:04:55.158
I am 103 years old.

70
00:04:55.159 --> 00:04:58.303
The Earthworms got on their bikes.

71
00:04:58.304 --> 00:05:00.805
"Hope to see you at the parade!"

72
00:05:00.806 --> 00:05:04.748
they called and headed back down the road.

73
00:05:04.749 --> 00:05:10.831
The next morning, Mrs. Penkov led the campers on a hike along Willow Creek.

74
00:05:10.832 --> 00:05:12.957
She showed them turtle eggs.

75
00:05:12.958 --> 00:05:16.775
She showed them a lizard sleeping in the sun.

76
00:05:16.776 --> 00:05:19.997
The campers picked wildflowers.

77
00:05:19.998 --> 00:05:23.288
Katie was thinking about Ms. Henderson.

78
00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:28.027
Did she walk along the creek when she was eight years old?

79
00:05:28.028 --> 00:05:31.148
What did the creek look like back then?

80
00:05:31.149 --> 00:05:34.132
Suddenly Emily grabbed Katie's arm.

81
00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:37.196
"Did you hear?" she whispered.

82
00:05:37.197 --> 00:05:42.995
"The Tornadoes are going to the senior home today to look for the oldest person."

83
00:05:42.996 --> 00:05:50.306
"HA!" said Katie. "They'll never find her there!"
